{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"EXT_ID:11537393 AND SRC:MED","internalQuery":"EXT_ID:11537393 AND SRC:MED","resultType":"CORE","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"11537393","source":"MED","pmid":"11537393","doi":"10.1016/0273-1177(89)90030-6","title":"Long-term experiments on man's stay in biological life-support system.","authorString":"Gitelson II, Terskov IA, Kovrov BG, Lisovskii GM, Okladnikov YuN, Sid'ko FYa, Trubachev IN, Shilenko MP, Alekseev SS, Pan'kova IM, Tirranen LS.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Gitelson II","lastName":"Gitelson","firstName":"I I","initials":"II","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Institute of Biophysics, USSR Academy of Sciences, Siberian Branch, Krasnoyarsk."}]}},{"fullName":"Terskov IA","lastName":"Terskov","firstName":"I A","initials":"IA"},{"fullName":"Kovrov BG","lastName":"Kovrov","firstName":"B G","initials":"BG"},{"fullName":"Lisovskii GM","lastName":"Lisovskii","firstName":"G M","initials":"GM"},{"fullName":"Okladnikov YuN","lastName":"Okladnikov YuN"},{"fullName":"Sid'ko FYa","lastName":"Sid'ko FYa"},{"fullName":"Trubachev IN","lastName":"Trubachev","firstName":"I N","initials":"IN"},{"fullName":"Shilenko MP","lastName":"Shilenko","firstName":"M P","initials":"MP"},{"fullName":"Alekseev SS","lastName":"Alekseev","firstName":"S S","initials":"SS"},{"fullName":"Pan'kova IM","lastName":"Pan'kova","firstName":"I M","initials":"IM"},{"fullName":"Tirranen LS","lastName":"Tirranen","firstName":"L S","initials":"LS"}]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"8","volume":"9","journalIssueId":550827,"dateOfPublication":"1989 ","monthOfPublication":0,"yearOfPublication":1989,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Adv Space Res","title":"Advances in space research : the official journal of the Committee on Space Research (COSPAR)","essn":"1879-1948","issn":"0273-1177","nlmid":"9878935","isoabbreviation":"Adv Space Res"},"printPublicationDate":"1989-01-01"},"pubYear":"1989","pageInfo":"65-71","abstractText":"We describe the experimental system having maximal possible closure of material recycling in an ecosystem, including people and plants, which was carried out in a hermetically sealed experimental complex \"BIOS-3\", 315 m2 in volume. The system included 2 experimentators and 3 phytotrons with plants (total sowing area of 63 m2). Plants were grown with round-the-clock lamp irradiation with 130 Wm-2 PAR intensity. The plants production was food for people. Water exchange of ecosystem, as wall as gas exchange, was fully closed excluding liquids and gas samples taken for chemical analysis outside the system. The total closure of material turnover constituted 91%. Health state of the crew was estimated before, during and after the experiment. A 5-months period did not affect their health. The experiments carried out prove that the closed ecosystem of \"man-plants\" is a prototype of a life-support system for long-term space expeditions.","affiliation":"Institute of Biophysics, USSR Academy of Sciences, Siberian Branch, Krasnoyarsk.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Journal Article"]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Humans"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Plants","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Triticum"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Crops, Agricultural"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Water"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Biomass"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Ecological Systems, Closed"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Air Conditioning","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"MT","qualifierName":"methods"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Life Support Systems","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualif